00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.350
Leah: When a child or young
person shows signs of experiencing

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.180
mental health concerns, usually
the first line treatments include

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.379
psychological therapies or medication.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:12.800
However, there are other approaches
that can help such as changing lifestyle

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.780
factors that influence mental health.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:19.570
Simple positive lifestyle changes that
can be made by Improving diet, increasing

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.290
exercise, prioritising sleep and rest,
and reaching out for help when needed.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.849
Rhiannon: Children and young people can
be encouraged to improve their fitness

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.060
by just getting out more walking or
playing as short bouts of activity can

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.000
provide an immediate elevation of mood.

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:38.090
Encouraging children and young
people to limit exposure to mobile

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.860
phones, computer and TV use or any
other substance if its excessive.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.179
Helping them to regulate their actions
can have positive benefits for sleep and

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.560
mood, and therefore their mental health.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.310
Leah: Spending time with nature such as
having a pet has many positive effects

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.350
and may also boost feelings of well-being.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.270
Exposure to sunshine helps
produce serotonin and boosts

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.840
vitamin D levels, which also has a
positive effect on mental health.

00:01:04.679 --> 00:01:08.159
Positive lifestyle changes aren't
a replacement for medication or

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.139
psychological therapy but something
people can undertake themselves,

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.529
on top of their treatment.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:19.600
Rhiannon: Social support is often
identified as an important component

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.789
of good relationships and strong
psychological health and involves having

00:01:22.789 --> 00:01:26.670
a network of family and friends that
can be turned to in times of need.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:31.990
Social support involves advice,
care, empathy and concern

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.980
anytime or when most needed.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.620
Others can help take care of physical
needs especially when people have

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.460
immediate needs that must be addressed
for example when a child has worries

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.990
about their workload for school.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:49.719
Some can provide informational support
providing guidance, advice, information,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.250
and mentoring especially important when
making decisions or big life changes.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.759
Leah: Being surrounded by people who
are caring and supportive helps children

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:05.069
and young people to deal more readily
with the stresses that life brings.

